	//   • FREE FUNCTIONS (E3006): these are the first listed modules since `Sleep.maxon` that declare a
	//     substantial set — nineteen across the three (seven `utf8*`, `hashString`, and grapheme.maxon's
	//     `findGraphemeEnd`/`findGraphemeStart`/`countGraphemes`/`byteIndexToGraphemeIndex`/
	//     `graphemeOffsetToBytePos`/`graphemeBreakProperty`/`isExtendedPictographic` plus four file-private
	//     helpers). Checked against `Parser.parseCallNamed`'s bare-name `if` chain AT THE CHAIN, which is what
	//     that rule's last bullet insists on: the chain claims `print trunc runProcess spawnReadLine subpSpawn
	//     subpReadLine subpReadErrLine subpWriteLine subpCloseStdin subpWait subpRelease floor ceil round sqrt
	//     abs min max`, and no name here is among them. ⚠⚠ **TWO OF THEM WERE, AND THAT IS THIS ENTRY'S WHOLE
	//     FIRST HALF.** `graphemeBreakProperty` and `isExtendedPictographic` stood in that chain until this
	//     rung, so listing this module WITHOUT retiring them would have loaded two declarations no call site
	//     could reach — `Sleep.maxon`'s defect exactly, and this file's rule says so in advance. They are
	//     retired (see the ✅ block in `Parser.maxon` where they were declared). Against the other listed
	//     modules there is no overlap either, checked AT THE SOURCE: `helpers/string/utf16.maxon`'s nine are
	//     all `utf16`-prefixed, `helpers/url/urlHelpers.maxon`'s eight all `url`-prefixed, and `Sleep.maxon`
	//     declares only `sleep`.
	//   • ⚠ These modules also CONSUME nothing the chain claims — `grapheme.maxon` calls `utf8DecodeAt` and
	//     `utf8ByteLengthAt`, which are its sibling's declarations, not builtins. That direction would be
	//     sound anyway (`Math.pow` consumes `floor`); it is checked because the two halves of the
	//     bare-builtin rule are different questions.
	//   • TYPE NAMES: none of the three declares a nominal `type`/`enum`/`union`/`interface` except
	//     `grapheme.maxon`'s file-private `GraphemeState`, which a user program spelling `GraphemeState` would
	//     shadow into the reserved space (A1s wave 2). No other listed module declares it.
	//   • TYPE-NAME-vs-BUILTIN, the one shape still SILENT: `GraphemeState` is on neither
	//     `TypeResolution.isCompilerOwnedTypeName` nor `builtinTypeNameTag`, and nothing in the compiler
	//     synthesizes a declaration of it — the SYNTHESIZED segmenter is a set of `__gr_`-prefixed Std bodies
